// The common prelude (issues/std-prelude-facade.md): the everyday names of
// the core modules, which every module later than this one in a run imports
// implicitly. A facade only (docs/modules-design.md §3.4): each name below is
// the declaration of the module it comes from, so a module that also imports
// that module directly sees one declaration, not two. The lists are chosen,
// not whole modules, so the core's lemma names (`nat`'s and `int`'s
// `le_trans`) stay out of every module's bare namespace; a module that wants
// them imports their module as before. The modules exported from are inside
// this facade's closure and so never import it themselves.
// The ordered-field tower, imported and not exported: no bare name of it
// enters an importer's namespace, but its modules are in the prelude's
// closure and so visible qualified-only everywhere (`names::common_reaches`).
// That is what the arithmetic tactics' own spellings need at a carrier whose
// instances a module reaches without naming their classes' modules
// (`semiring::CommRingOfInt`, `ordered_field::OrderedField`, the certificate
// lemmas they cite): `import rat; import linarith;` is enough for `linarith`
// at `Rat` (issues/linarith-rat-without-ordered-field-import.md).
import ordered_field;

export logic::{Not, And, Or, Iff, Exists, DecEq};
export bool::{Bool, Decide, decide, decide_bit};
export option::{Option};
export list::{List};
export pair::{Pair};
export algebra::{Numeral, Default, Cmp, Semigroup, Monoid, CommMonoid, Group};
export char::{Char};
export string::{String};
